btBatchedConstraints: a body at the grid's max corner is clamped into the last cell

Jahshaka's change, BULLET-BATCHING-1 fix round (2026-10-19). A genuine upstream
defect: bulletphysics/bullet3 at the pinned 3.25 (2c204c49e), file
src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp — the second of
the batch grid's two rounding faults (0001 is the first); an upstream PR is
owed for both.

The bug
-------
setupSpatialGridBatchesMt sizes the grid as
`gridDim = int(1.0 + gridExtent / gridCellSize)` (upstream :927-929) and puts
each dynamic body in `int((p - bboxMin) * invGridCellSize)` (:951-955),
invGridCellSize = fl(1 / gridCellSize) (:945), then asserts
`coords < gridDim` (:956-958). For the body AT bboxMax the two are computed
differently: fl(E / c) for the dimension, fl(E * fl(1 / c)) for the coordinate.
When E / c falls a few ulps under an integer k, the division rounds under k
(gridDim = k) while the product rounds up to k (coord = k = gridDim): the
assert fails.
  * Debug: an abort. Measured on a float replica of this code
    (spikes/bullet-batching-1/reader-fuzz/: dim.cpp, rate.cpp): ~3.6e-7 per
    axis per batch setup for an unstructured pile — about one abort every few
    hours of one large batched island at 60 Hz. 0001's epsilon neither causes
    nor fixes it; it surfaced when the shipped world turned batching on.
  * Release: harmless by accident — assignConstraintsToGridBatches clamps the
    CHUNK coordinate (:765), folding the overflow cell into the last chunk.

The fix
-------
Clamp the three coordinates to gridDim - 1 right after they are computed.
The clamped body sits at the max corner; its constraint partners lie within
one cell extent of it (0001), i.e. in the last cell or the one below, so a
constraint still spans at most one cell and the phase/batch assignment stays
body-disjoint. The asserts stay (they still guard the lower bound).

--- a/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp
+++ b/src/BulletDynamics/ConstraintSolver/btBatchedConstraints.cpp
@@ -958,6 +958,12 @@
 			coords.m_ints[0] = int(v.x());
 			coords.m_ints[1] = int(v.y());
 			coords.m_ints[2] = int(v.z());
+			// The body at bboxMax lands ON gridDim when fl(gridExtent / cellSize) (gridDim, above) rounds a few ulps under
+			// an integer while fl(extent * fl(1 / cellSize)) here rounds up to it (Jahshaka bullet-patches/0002): clamp
+			// into the last cell. Its partners are in the last cell or the one below, so a pair still spans <= 1 cell.
+			coords.m_ints[0] = btMin(coords.m_ints[0], gridDim[0] - 1);
+			coords.m_ints[1] = btMin(coords.m_ints[1], gridDim[1] - 1);
+			coords.m_ints[2] = btMin(coords.m_ints[2], gridDim[2] - 1);
 			btAssert(coords.m_ints[0] >= 0 && coords.m_ints[0] < gridDim[0]);
 			btAssert(coords.m_ints[1] >= 0 && coords.m_ints[1] < gridDim[1]);
 			btAssert(coords.m_ints[2] >= 0 && coords.m_ints[2] < gridDim[2]);
